[2026-03-15T09:35:55.579Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EnB6uhLcgBhdLXr5NJU4dM","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Reference\n\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and troubleshoot issues. Here's what you need to know:\n\n## Quick Start\n\n**Install** via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n**Authenticate** by setting your API key from https://app.replay.io settings:\n```sh\nexport REPLAY_API_KEY=your_key\n```\n\n## Key Commands\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** - Launch Replay Browser and record a session\n- **`replayio list`** - Display all local recordings\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** - Upload recordings to Replay\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** - Delete local recordings\n- **`replayio login/logout`** - Manage account access\n- **`replayio info`** - Check installed versions\n\n## Common Workflow\n\nRecord your app, then upload the session:\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\nUse `-h` or `--help` with any command for detailed options. For debugging recorded applications, you can integrate the Replay MCP Server with Claude using the provided configuration."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1be6b722-4a09-4a27-a831-da3ee866becd","uuid":"4024c6a9-5e22-4407-8529-d0b778b210e0","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Reference\n\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and troubleshoot issues. Here's what you need to know:\n\n## Quick Start\n\n**Install** via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n**Authenticate** by setting your API key from https://app.replay.io settings:\n```sh\nexport REPLAY_API_KEY=your_key\n```\n\n## Key Commands\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** - Launch Replay Browser and record a session\n- **`replayio list`** - Display all local recordings\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** - Upload recordings to Replay\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** - Delete local recordings\n- **`replayio login/logout`** - Manage account access\n- **`replayio info`** - Check installed versions\n\n## Common Workflow\n\nRecord your app, then upload the session:\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\nUse `-h` or `--help` with any command for detailed options. For debugging recorded applications, you can integrate the Replay MCP Server with Claude using the provided configuration.","durationMs":3382,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T09:35:56.378Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012XfvWYrUsi4sm7xETuD98p","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser activity. The documentation organizes investigation into three key phases:\n\n**Investigation Framework:**\nThe guide emphasizes avoiding premature conclusions by: \"Frame your task in the form of a question that you need to answer\" then using exploratory and explanatory tools systematically.\n\n**Tool Categories:**\n\n*Exploratory tools* discover what happened:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline tools (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source analysis (find and search code files)\n\n*Explanatory tools* clarify why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking to understand cause-and-effect relationships\n- Detail tools providing variable values, DOM element properties, and component trees\n\n**Key Concepts:**\nThe recording functions as a database with two fundamental units: \"Point\" (specific execution moments) and \"Element\" (persistent DOM references independent of time).\n\n**Practical Recommendation:**\nThe guide suggests using the Logpoint tool to \"see the value of the same expression whenever a statement executed\" to identify unexpected behavior patterns, then drill deeper from there."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1be6b722-4a09-4a27-a831-da3ee866becd","uuid":"17599378-7838-41a8-a379-47bc46241512","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser activity. The documentation organizes investigation into three key phases:\n\n**Investigation Framework:**\nThe guide emphasizes avoiding premature conclusions by: \"Frame your task in the form of a question that you need to answer\" then using exploratory and explanatory tools systematically.\n\n**Tool Categories:**\n\n*Exploratory tools* discover what happened:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline tools (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source analysis (find and search code files)\n\n*Explanatory tools* clarify why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking to understand cause-and-effect relationships\n- Detail tools providing variable values, DOM element properties, and component trees\n\n**Key Concepts:**\nThe recording functions as a database with two fundamental units: \"Point\" (specific execution moments) and \"Element\" (persistent DOM references independent of time).\n\n**Practical Recommendation:**\nThe guide suggests using the Logpoint tool to \"see the value of the same expression whenever a statement executed\" to identify unexpected behavior patterns, then drill deeper from there.","durationMs":3588,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
